{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>We will go up, and we will cut it off.</b> A verb in the active voice, so that it is cut off because of us. And the meaning concerns Jerusalem, therefore [read כן] and we will split it open:" "<b>The son of Tabeal.</b> Some say that it is by letter-substitution ramla, and he is the son of Remaliah. This is nonsense, [for] since he mentioned at the outset the son of Remaliah, and he says with Aram and we will set up a king — one says the good to us, and the word אל is nothing but negation, as if they said את בן טוב לא. The correct view is that he is the name of a great officer of Israel or of Aram:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The bracketed [צ\"ל כן] is a scribal correction note indicating כי should read כן; translated accordingly.", 1 "The word אל is here taken by some as a negative particle (= 'not'), producing the reading את בן טוב לא; the transliteration of the divine name is avoided since Ibn Ezra explicitly denies that reading."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:35.544392376Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}